==English==
[[File:Spermaceti candle and oil.jpg|thumb|a sample of spermaceti wax, a spermaceti candle, and a jar of sperm oil]]
[[File:Sperm whale head anatomy (transverse + sagittal).svg|thumb|sperm oil inside the head of a sperm whale]]

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|sperma|t1=sperm|cētī|t2=of the whale|pos2=genitive of {{m|la|cētus}}|lang1=la|lang2=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌspɜːməˈsiːti/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-spermaceti.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/spɚməˈsiːti/|/spɚməˈsɛti/|/spɚməˈsɪti/|q3=obsolete, proscribed|a=GA}}<ref>{{R:Meredith EES|Spermaceti|42}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{senseid|en|Q369682}} A [[wax]] obtained from the head of [[sperm whale]]s and used to make [[cosmetics]], etc; humans separate it out from [[sperm oil]].
#: {{hyper|en|whale oil<id:Q1053334>|<|oil#Noun|lipid#Noun}}
#: {{hol|en|sperm oil<id:Q7576374><!--spermaceti is a [[w:fraction (chemistry)|fraction]] of [[sperm oil]] that humans separate out-->}}
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|[[s:Moby-Dick (1851) US edition/Chapter 6|chapter 6]]|passage=You must go to New Bedford to see a brilliant wedding; for, they say, they have reservoirs of oil in every house, and every night recklessly burn their lengths in '''spermaceti''' candles.}}
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|[[s:Moby-Dick (1851) US edition/Chapter 77|chapter 77]]|passage=Moreover, as that of Heidelburgh was always replenished with the most excellent of the wines of the Rhenish valleys, so the tun of the whale contains by far the most precious of all his oily vintages; namely, the highly-prized '''spermaceti''', in its absolutely pure, limpid, and odoriferous state.}}

